(7779151, 1293767, 91496, '<td valign="top">
The color is pumped up a bit as I shot in raw and that is always a bit muted.  Adding in contrast to bring out the feather details also darkens the color as well.  Keep in mind the body is mostly pink and the neck is the deeper red.  This close-up pose really has a lot of the neck, hence the red dominates.  Traditional full body poses highlight the pink, which is why they are commonly called pink flamingos.  I was real lucky and got great sunshine on them.  Later in the day as I shot other animals it was a dull gray overcast.</td>', 'The color is pumped up a bit as I shot in raw and that is always a bit muted.  Adding in contrast to bring out the feather details also darkens the color as well.  Keep in mind the body is mostly pink and the neck is the deeper red.  This close-up pose really has a lot of the neck, hence the red dominates.  Traditional full body poses highlight the pink, which is why they are commonly called pink flamingos.  I was real lucky and got great sunshine on them.  Later in the day as I shot other animals it was a dull gray overcast.', '2025-04-05 11:48:56.000000', NULL, 0),
